CONTRACT DEFINITION:
1. RESEARCH NOTE: Verified at file-injector.ts — injectFiles is at L1114 with signature `injectFiles(text, imagesIn, ctx, bareAt = false)`. The processTokenStream call is at L1184 (scans #@ files). The state.count === 0 early return is at L1186. The input handler is at L1248-1271; the pre-check is L1255 (`if (!event.text?.includes('#@')) return { action: 'continue' }`), the injectFiles call is L1257. Module-level cfg is at L1227. See plan/010_8645157f3bf5/architecture/system_context.md §2 for exact verified line numbers.
2. INPUT: P1.M1.T2.S1 provides injectUrl(url, state, ctx). P1.M1.T1.S3 provides URL_INJECT_RE + URL_SHAPE_RE. P1.M1.T1.S2 provides enableUrls on FileInjectorConfig. The existing cleanToken (L91) strips trailing punctuation from URL tokens. The existing State.injectedSet (L465) is a Set<string> for dedup.
3. LOGIC: Three changes:
   (A) injectFiles signature (L1114): add `enableUrls = true` as a trailing param → `injectFiles(text, imagesIn, ctx, bareAt = false, enableUrls = true)`. This mirrors the existing bareAt seam pattern. Default true for direct unit tests; the handler passes the real value.
   (B) URL loop in injectFiles: AFTER the processTokenStream call (L1184) and BEFORE the state.count === 0 check (L1186), insert:
     ```ts
     if (enableUrls) {
       for (const m of text.matchAll(URL_INJECT_RE)) {
         const tok = cleanToken(m[2]);
         if (tok && URL_SHAPE_RE.test(tok)) {
           const abs = /^https?:\/\//i.test(tok) ? tok : 'https://' + tok;
           if (!state.injectedSet.has(abs)) {
             state.injectedSet.add(abs);
             await injectUrl(abs, state, ctx);
           }
         }
       }
     }
     ```
     This shares state (blocks, details, images, injectedSet, remaining, count) so budget/dedup/count span BOTH triggers. Dedup by absolute URL form (#example.com and #https://example.com collapse to one). The state.count++ in injectUrl means the L1186 early-return correctly stays open when only URLs injected.
   (C) Input handler (L1255): broaden the pre-check from `!event.text?.includes('#@')` to `!event.text?.includes('#')` (both triggers contain #). At L1257, pass the new arg: `injectFiles(event.text, event.images ?? [], ctx, cfg.markdownBareAtImports === true, cfg.enableUrls !== false)`. The verbatim-prompt return (L1271: `text: event.text`) is UNCHANGED — failed URL tokens stay verbatim exactly like failed #@ tokens. The notify at L1266 already counts state.count (includes URL successes).
4. OUTPUT: injectFiles now accepts enableUrls (5th param, default true). The input handler passes cfg.enableUrls !== false. URL-only prompts reach the engine. Both triggers share state. No #@ behavior change.
5. DOCS: [Mode A] JSDoc on the new enableUrls param in injectFiles + a comment block on the URL loop explaining the shared-state design and the cleanToken + URL_SHAPE_RE + dedup pipeline. This rides WITH the work.
